WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.175
Welcome to Horizon
installer training, Part 6.

2
00:00:05.555 --> 00:00:07.059
Test before you leave.

3
00:00:07.509 --> 00:00:11.467
By the end, you will know the two
tests we run on every circuit,

4
00:00:11.467 --> 00:00:14.377
and how to read a pass,
a tight, or a fail.

5
00:00:14.827 --> 00:00:18.223
You will also know how to fill in
the test sheet for the job file.

6
00:00:19.573 --> 00:00:22.877
Here is the rule. If you did not
measure it, it is not finished.

7
00:00:23.327 --> 00:00:26.015
Every job gets tested
before the truck leaves.

8
00:00:26.465 --> 00:00:30.047
Two readings on every circuit.
Amps, and volts at the end.

9
00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:34.984
Both are taken on Pure White, because
that is the hardest the system ever works.

10
00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:37.147
It takes about ten minutes.

11
00:00:37.597 --> 00:00:41.573
Why Pure White? On PW, all
three colours turn on at once.

12
00:00:41.573 --> 00:00:46.148
A run can be fine on red or blue,
and still overload on white.

13
00:00:47.498 --> 00:00:49.641
Test A. Amps on every circuit.

14
00:00:50.091 --> 00:00:53.882
Step 1. Set the whole
system to PW, full bright.

15
00:00:54.332 --> 00:00:59.586
Step 2. Clamp the meter around the
positive feeder of one circuit, at the box.

16
00:01:00.036 --> 00:01:02.004
One wire only. Not both.

17
00:01:02.454 --> 00:01:05.200
Step 3. Read it, and write it down.

18
00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:07.700
Then do the same on every circuit.

19
00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:12.068
Every reading goes on the test sheet.
You will see it at the end of this part.

20
00:01:13.418 --> 00:01:15.201
Test B. Volts at the end.

21
00:01:15.651 --> 00:01:21.276
Step 1. Stay on PW. Meter the supply
output. It should read about 24 volts.

22
00:01:21.726 --> 00:01:24.693
Step 2. Meter at the
last light in that group.

23
00:01:25.143 --> 00:01:29.108
Step 3. It must not drop below 22.8 volts.

24
00:01:29.558 --> 00:01:33.431
That is a 5% drop, and 5% is our limit.

25
00:01:33.881 --> 00:01:36.859
Then do the same at the
last light of every group.

26
00:01:38.209 --> 00:01:42.372
Now, reading the results.
First, amps on PW.

27
00:01:42.822 --> 00:01:47.507
Under 3.6 amps is a pass.
Write it down, and move on.

28
00:01:47.957 --> 00:01:50.241
3.6 to 4.0 amps is tight. It works,

29
00:01:50.241 --> 00:01:54.081
but no lights get added to
this circuit later. Note it.

30
00:01:54.531 --> 00:01:58.078
Over 4.0 amps is a fail. Too many lights.

31
00:01:58.528 --> 00:02:02.052
Split it, and add an injection.
Do not leave it like this.

32
00:02:02.502 --> 00:02:05.930
Remember. Tight means it works,
but that circuit is full.

33
00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:08.766
Note it, so nobody adds
lights to it later.

34
00:02:10.116 --> 00:02:12.073
Next, volts at the last light.

35
00:02:12.523 --> 00:02:16.593
22.8 volts or more is
a pass. Write it down.

36
00:02:17.043 --> 00:02:21.360
Under 22.8 volts is a fail.
The injection is too far away.

37
00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.620
Move it closer, or add one.

38
00:02:24.070 --> 00:02:27.629
And if a breaker trips on
PW, that is a fail too.

39
00:02:28.079 --> 00:02:32.009
Too many lights. Count them.
It is almost always over 70.

40
00:02:32.459 --> 00:02:37.298
Remember from Part 3. Far-end lights
that look dim or yellow are voltage drop.

41
00:02:37.298 --> 00:02:40.836
The fix is a closer injection,
never a bigger supply.

42
00:02:42.442 --> 00:02:45.710
Last, the test sheet.
Leave it with the job file.

43
00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:49.387
One row for each circuit.
Write down the lights on it,

44
00:02:49.387 --> 00:02:52.506
the amps on PW, and the
volts at the last light.

45
00:02:52.956 --> 00:02:55.632
Then mark each one, pass or fail.

46
00:02:56.082 --> 00:02:59.734
Fill in the address, the
installer, and the date.

47
00:03:00.184 --> 00:03:03.232
Remember. If you did not
measure it, it is not finished.

48
00:03:03.682 --> 00:03:06.546
The sheet has a row for
every circuit on the board,

49
00:03:06.546 --> 00:03:10.166
one to six. Fill in a row for
each light circuit you tested.

50
00:03:11.516 --> 00:03:12.579
Let's lock it in.

51
00:03:13.029 --> 00:03:15.912
If you did not measure
it, it is not finished.

52
00:03:15.912 --> 00:03:18.794
Two readings on every circuit, both on PW.

53
00:03:19.244 --> 00:03:23.708
Test A. Clamp the positive
feeder only, at the box.

54
00:03:23.708 --> 00:03:27.284
Under 3.6 amps passes. Over 4.0 fails.

55
00:03:27.734 --> 00:03:34.184
Test B. About 24 volts at the supply, and
at least 22.8 volts at the last light.

56
00:03:34.634 --> 00:03:37.747
Fail on amps? Split it,
and add an injection.

57
00:03:37.747 --> 00:03:41.664
Fail on volts? Move the
injection closer, or add one.

58
00:03:42.114 --> 00:03:45.243
Fill in the test sheet, and
leave it with the job file.

59
00:03:45.693 --> 00:03:48.673
Next, take the Part 6
quiz. Then in Part 7,

60
00:03:48.673 --> 00:03:52.526
the last part, we look at
old systems and retrofits.
